- **C1. Delta, provenance, NO LOOSENING, hygiene (cheap, first).** FAIL: the head other than `867f3402` or more than one commit above `c2f0b789`; a path other than the test file in `git diff --name-only c2f0b789 867f3402` (and `pulls/95/files` for the commit: compare `c2f0b789...867f3402` by `gh api -X GET compare`, and the merge ref's tree vs main in your clone: the PR still = the same two paths; control: a planted path); any byte of `apps/api/src/**`, `packages/**`, `apps/web/**`, `scripts/**`, `docker/**`, `.github/**`, `DEPLOY.md`, a package file, lockfile, config, `harness.ts`, `flows.ts`, `b144-set-target-pending.db.test.ts` differing between `c2f0b789` and the head (blobs by `rev-parse`; control: two different blobs differ); `git diff --numstat c2f0b789 867f3402` other than `245 0`. **No loosening, no rename, no reorder (your program, not the builder's `checks.py`):** extract every `describe(`/`it(` title and every existing row's body text from the file at `c2f0b789` and at the head; the nine old rows' titles AND bodies must be byte-identical and in the same relative order; **names lost 0, added 8** against `c2f0b789` and against main's tree (the file is new at main: lost 0 there too), no duplicate title (controls: one title dropped from a copy reports lost 1, one character edited reports a body difference, a planted duplicate reports 1). `git diff c2f0b789 867f3402` removed lines: 0 (control: a scratch edit makes it 1); read the added lines of the helper `completeSetup` (one optional parameter and one spread line) and prove by `tsc` of the file (scratch tsconfig under `.tools/b743`, control: `--listFilesOnly` lists the file, a planted type error gives rc 2) that the nine old call sites compile unchanged and send the same bodies. **Hygiene** over the 245 added lines, the commit message and the PR title (read whole): person or client name from a list you derive at run time (never written to a file), card slug, tab, bidi (a planted U+202E built at run time fires), non-ASCII 0 (control: a planted U+00E9 counts 1), `skip|only|todo|skipIf|runIf|retry|xit|xdescribe|test.fails|expect.soft|console\.` (control: a planted `it.skip` fires; `only` can sit inside prose: read it), a percent figure, a Jira key or work number in the COMMIT MESSAGE (MEASURED-BY-DRAFTER: the message names none; the file's titles carry `B712 PCOMP-24`: a Note, the file's habit), trailer `Co-Authored-By` count 1 (control 0), author and committer identities of the two commits equal (count distinct identities; quote no name). Fixtures synthetic ("(fictional)"); the credential-shaped string built from parts at run time, never a literal (gitleaks, C7).
- **C2. THE CENSUS, re-derived from source (the heart, do this first of the heavy work).** FAIL: a refusal before the new call that you can name and that the table below misses; a refusal you classify "not movable" without proof; the builder's count 12 wrong in either direction. **Property first:** a "refusal before the new check" is any `throw` (or call that can throw) on the path from the request to the first line of `refuseTargetAlreadyChosen`'s call in `completeExpertSetup`, including inside the helpers it calls (`refuseCredentialText`, `requireIfMatch`, `expertSetupPending`, `refuseBlank`, `refuseRepeatedApprovers`, `refuseUnlinkedApprovers`, `policyTargetOf`, `refuseStalePin` / `versionPins` / `refuseUnpinned`, `lockDraft` / `editableVersion` / `engagementRow`), the operation wrapper `inEngagement` / `withRequestTransaction` / `authorize` / `scopeToOwnEngagement`, and the route's request schema. Print the census as a table `n | refusal | source file:line at the head | status | code | detail source | movable-ahead-of-by-the-new-check y/n | proof` over the raw files at the head (frame: the files named; count of `throw`/`conflict(`/`unprocessable(`/`invalid(`/`notFound(` sites in them, control: a planted site in a scratch copy raises the count by 1). A refusal that cannot be reached ahead of by the new call (it supplies the data the call needs: `engagementRow` for `policy_id`; the pre-handler 404 / 403 / schema 400) is "equivalent by construction": show why by reading, and show by your request prober that the request never reaches the handler's new call. Then print the **row-to-refusal map**: for each movable refusal, the new-file row that exercises it, by title and line, and the assertions (status, code, detail, row-equal digest) that row makes; a movable refusal with no row = Major of the class (G-3).
- **C3. The swaps (the red-proofs, yours), at the FIXED file and, as the control that reproduces the defect, at the OLD file.** In `wt-b743-mut` (never committed; plain text swaps you write from THIS brief's words, anchor count 1 each, one mutant file per swap, each restore `cmp`-equal to the head file; a mutant that does not load or typecheck is reported as that, never as a kill; a failing assertion is quoted from the TEXT reporter). **Two families, so a refusal cannot hide behind the other:** `A_x` = the target-already-chosen call (with `policyTargetOf` computed there, guarded as at the head) placed immediately BEFORE refusal x; `T_x` = refusal x moved textually to just AFTER the new call (the call keeps its place; defined for every x including the credential refusal, which `A_x` cannot reach because the call needs `current.policy_id`); and the **block family** `B_x` = the whole key-handling block (`policyTargetOf`, `refuseStalePin`, `lockDraft`, the call) placed before refusal x (your own S11c is `B_x` for x = the blank-environment refusal; write it from the property, not from the builder). For every movable x of the C2 table: `A_x`, `T_x`, `B_x`; plus the within-block orders (the call before `lockDraft`, before `refuseStalePin`, before `policyTargetOf`/key test), `M1` (the call deleted), `S4` (the `target !== null` guard dropped: the keyless row red), `S5` (refuse only when the held key differs: the same-key row red), `S8` (the helper's sentence changed by one character), and controls that must stay green (a trailing comment; whitespace inside the guard; an `A_x` that changes nothing, e.g. the call placed where it already is). **Predict in writing BEFORE each run which rows go red** (each new row red BY NAME under every swap that moves the check ahead of its own refusal; the order row red under the stale-pin, If-Match and unknown-key swaps; controls 0 red). Run every swap on **the new file plus the 14 existing API files that call `expert-setup` or `policy-target`** (`grep -l -E 'expert-setup|policy-target' apps/api/test` at the head yields them; the builder's STATUS names 14 at B724's line 30 count): 15 files per swap; batch behind one throwaway postgres. At the **OLD nine-row file** (the file at `c2f0b789` copied into the mut tree) run `B_x` for x in {not pending, blank environment, blank policy name, repeated, unlinked} and the lockDraft swap: they must be GREEN (the defect, reproduced by your own swap before any fixed-file run; if any is red there, the finding B724-1 was wrong or the old file differs: say so). **Every swap that stays green under the fixed file's 17 rows and the 14 neighbours = the row set cannot fail there: it is a Major of the class unless your request prober shows it changes no answer of any request (an EQUIVALENT swap: say why, with the probe's table).** For each red, print the first failing assertion: it must be the row's own expectation (the API answered 409 `POLICY_TARGET_ALREADY_CHOSEN` where the row expects its own status and code) and not a harness error, a 500, a timeout or a bad plant (a red for a wrong reason = Major of the class, G-3). Controls: unmutated 0 red (ran 17 + the neighbours), a trailing comment 0 red.
- **C4. The new rows are valid, isolated and stable.** FAIL: a new row green at base for a wrong reason, a new row that leaves state behind, a row that depends on another. (a) **At base:** the new file run against main's `engagements.ts` (a tree `wt-b743-main` + the new file): expect 13 red of 17 (the five of B724 plus the 8 new rows' step (d), each "expected 200 to be 409"-shaped or the tripwire row's contract-check 500) and the first half of each new row (the refusal's own answer) passing; print by title with the failing assertion; a red whose cause is not "the call answered 200 and moved the key" is not evidence. (b) **Plant validity** (the two rows that plant states no API makes): prove the draft detach restores `pc.policy_version` byte-equal (your state dumper, before the plant and after `reattachDraft`), that `SET LOCAL session_replication_role` does not outlive the transaction (`SHOW session_replication_role` on `h.admin` after the row, expected `origin`), that the TEMP table is gone after the row, that a row failing midway cannot leave the draft detached for the next row (read the `try/catch` and `afterEach`/cleanup: if a failing assertion between `detachDraft` and `reattachDraft` leaves the database without its draft for later rows, say so with a measured example by an `-mut` edit of the file's assertion, never committed: a **Minor** if later rows then fail for that reason alone), and that the in-review plant is a state the guard trigger allows and an API route can also produce (read `lockDraft`'s callers; if no API route produces it, a Note). (c) **Isolation:** the new file alone 3 consecutive runs (17 of 17, rc 0); each row alone by `-t` (17 of 17); the new describe alone; the file run with its two describes in reverse order by an `-mut` edit (a scratch copy; rows must not depend on order). (d) **The refusal halves write nothing (your dumper, not the builder's `written()`):** for each of the 8 new rows, the state digest of every `pc.*` table of the tenant equal before and after the refusal half AND after the success-shaped 409 half, engagement and version ETags equal, the placeholder approver present; control: a request that succeeds (the keyless set-up) changes the digest, and the same request at main (the new rows' step (d) at base) changes it. Read what `written()` covers (static) and say which tables it misses, if any; a missed table the dumper shows changing in a refusal = Major of the class.
- **C5. The differential and the unchanged-product proof.** FAIL: any request whose answer differs between the head with the new rows and main's tree other than the 6 cells B724 recorded (pending start holding a target x `completeExpertSetup` with a valid key: 200 at main, 409 at the head); any product byte. The product is byte-equal to the gated head (blob `fd072db6` at both shas), so B724's C2 (routes, database census, tripwire, black-box sweep), C3 (sentence hashes, new words), C4 (175-cell differential) and C5 (race) are **CARRIED by blob equality, not re-run: state it plainly under NOT TESTED with the blob proof and the control (two different blobs differ)**. What you DO re-run is the request prober of C2/C3 at the head: for every movable refusal's request, the head answers with that refusal's own status/code/detail and, with the fault removed, 409 `POLICY_TARGET_ALREADY_CHOSEN` whose `detail` hashes (sha256) equal to `setPolicyTarget`'s sentence at the head (control: a one-character edit changes the hash and the program says so); the answers of the 8 first halves are EQUAL at main's tree and the head's (the refusals existed before), and the 8 second halves differ (200 at main, 409 at the head). A mismatch in the first halves = a changed answer = Major of the class.
- **C6. Tests and suites (Composer heavy rules).** CI predicates: Composer has no test workflow; `scripts/ci.sh` runs every step, a step PASS only on exit 0 (the node step `node: lint, format, typecheck, build, test (--network none)`; the db step `scripts/test-db.sh` runs `npx vitest run --config packages/db/vitest.config.ts && npx vitest run --config apps/api/vitest.db.config.ts` in a network-less container against the digest-pinned `postgres:16`, inspect locally, never pull; re-read the lines and write the pass predicate in STATUS). At the head tree in `pc-b743-node:head`: the new file alone **17 of 17 rc 0** (C4c); the **whole API db group** (`apps/api/vitest.db.config.ts`) at the head tree, at main `8347f91b`, and at the **merge-equal tree** (main + the PR's two paths, built in a throwaway index so its `write-tree` is compared with the merge ref's tree `2baf91a1`): **head tree = 81 files / 1509 tests (the B724 head-tree 1501 + 8; the head tree lacks main's `b626-date-rule-rows` file), main = your own baseline (B724 measured 81 / 1522), merge-equal = main + 1 file + 17 tests = 82 / 1539**, failures 0 (print yours; the builder's 81/1509 is a claim). The **unit chain** (`unit.sh ci`: whole-repo `npm run lint`, `npm run format:check`, `npm run typecheck`, `npm run build`, then `vitest run`, the contract file included) rc 0 each on the head and on main (the file is a database test, so the unit counts do not move: 311 files / 3107 tests, 3106 passed + 1 skipped, RELAYED; a rc non-zero only on the head = Major); `prettier --check` and `eslint` on the one path alone (controls: a scratch file with bad spacing and an unused variable gives rc 1 and rc 1). The `packages/db` group is NOT re-run (no `packages/db` byte; say so under NOT TESTED). A red only under load and green re-run alone at load1 below 6 is a load artefact: record both.
- **C7. CodeQL, checks, merge, overlap, claims, secrets.** FAIL: a state you cannot name. `check-runs --paginate` on the head at start, mid and verdict with the time (expected at the draft: 2 runs `completed` / `failure`, each annotated "The job was not started because recent account payments have failed or your spending limit needs to be increased"): **read the annotations of each run (`check-runs/<id>/annotations`) and the timestamps before grading; a `failure` whose annotation is that sentence is the product owner's billing pause, not a finding on the code.** If a run is `queued` or `in_progress` at a read, poll every 60 s up to 40 minutes beyond your last heavy job and never conclude from a partial set. `code-scanning/analyses?ref=refs/pull/95/head` (`commit_sha`, `results_count`, `error`; control `ref=refs/heads/main` returns rows): the head `867f3402` NOT scanned unless a row names it; alerts in ALL states on `refs/pull/95/head`, `refs/pull/95/merge` and main (dismissed equal at start and verdict; you never dismiss). **The CI grade is `CI pending: not scanned (job not started)`, a condition: never "clean", never "failed".** Added source lines: none (test code only). In the added test lines list every `query(` call (expected: `h.admin.query` with bound parameters or fixed statements; template literals with `${}` in SQL 0; control: a planted line is flagged); no `RegExp`, `readFile`, `eval` (control: a planted line counts 1); the credential-shaped string is built from parts at run time (read line 312). **Merge in YOUR plain clone:** `git clone --no-hardlinks --no-checkout '<project>/2_Project_Files' '<project>/.tools/b743/repo'` (never `--shared`; push URL `DISABLED-no-push`; prove the shared `.git/objects` mtime and `for-each-ref` count unchanged), ONE explicit fetch `'+refs/heads/main:refs/remotes/origin/main' '+refs/pull/95/head:refs/remotes/origin/pr95'` (no `--prune`; retry a `Permission denied (publickey)` 5x): **re-read main with `ls-remote` first (it was `8347f91b` at the draft) and say if it moved**; `rev-list --left-right --count origin/main...origin/pr95` = `1 2` while main is `8347f91b` (the head's parent chain is two commits above the PR's old parent; derive and print yours); `git merge-tree --write-tree origin/main origin/pr95` rc 0 and its tree compared with the merge ref's tree `2baf91a1` (equal while main is unmoved); the merge result's diff against main = the two paths = `pulls/95/files`; control: a scratch branch changing the SAME lines of `engagements.ts` differently conflicts (rc 1). `pulls/95` `mergeable` / `mergeable_state` and `refs/pull/95/merge` parents + tree at start and verdict. **Overlap by GET:** `pulls/<n>/files --paginate` for #94, #91, #86, #85 (and any PR opened since) against the two paths by `/usr/bin/grep -c -x -F` (controls: self-compare of #95 lists 2, a planted shared path found), plus every live `b6*`/`b7*` branch by `compare` (squash-merged history branches are listed, not stops); if a B742 builder is live, name its branch and its path from your side. **Claims (the builder STATUS B737, line by line):** a `PRIOR WORK` section exists (heading found by `/usr/bin/grep -n -i`), 8 rows added, 20 swaps as predicted, the 13-red M1, API db 81/1509, unit 311/3107, names lost 0 added 8, NEW WORDS 0, "removed lines 0", the stray `rm -f` disclosure (a Note), the same author identity. A claim your run contradicts = Major if it hides a defect, Minor if only a number. gitleaks `/opt/homebrew/bin/gitleaks`: a RANDOM `ghp_`-shaped canary written at run time into a scratch directory rc 1 FIRST (typed into no file of the project), then `c2f0b789..867f3402` AND `8347f91b..867f3402` rc 0, chained with `&&` in `bash -c`. Evidence and `.tools/b743/` hold 0 non-ASCII bytes in your own files (`LC_ALL=C /usr/bin/grep -c '[^ -~]'`, control: a planted byte counts 1; byte copies of product source are the exception, named), no person's name, no card slug, no four-underscore run. At the end: nothing of yours running, lock released by move into `quarantine/locks/`, containers, networks, images and trees named with state, every scratch change restored byte-equal (sha256), refs before/after in your clone (added only `refs/remotes/origin/*`, removed 0), no ref on origin, no PR comment, no push, `lsof -nP -iTCP:9990-9999 -sTCP:LISTEN` rc 1.
Priority if short: C2 and C3 (the census and the swaps: the heart), then C1 (cheap, first in time), C4, C5, C6, C7. A verdict from a gate that did not finish C2, C3 (the fixed-file table over the 15 files), C4a-c and the new file's runs at the head is conditional and never a clean GO.

## GRADING (binding; the ONE table; capability decides)
- **G-1 delta and no-loosening (C1).** A path beyond the one test path since `c2f0b789`, or a byte of `apps/api/src`, the contract, `apps/web`, `packages/db`, `DEPLOY.md`, a package/config/lock file, `harness.ts`, `flows.ts` or an existing test file = **Blocker**; an existing row's title or body changed, reordered or removed, an assertion loosened, a removed line = **Major, class**; a second commit above `867f3402` or a moved head = STOP; a person's name, real customer name, secret or decision-card slug in an added line or message = **Blocker**; a work number or ticket key in the commit message = **Minor**; work numbers in the new titles (the file's habit) = **Note**.
- **G-2 the census (C2).** A refusal before the new call with no row = **Major, class**; a census entry classified "not movable" without proof and in fact movable = **Major, class**; the builder's count wrong by a refusal that a swap moves the check ahead of unseen = **Major, class**; a count off only in wording = **Minor**.
- **G-3 closure and the rows (C3, C4).** A swap that moves the check ahead of a refusal and stays green under every row and neighbour, and changes an answer of the prober = **Major, class**; a swap unobservable by any instrument (equivalent by construction, shown) = **Note**; a row red under no swap, or red at base or under a swap for a wrong reason = **Major, class**; a new row green at base on its second half (step (d) not red at main) = **Major, class**; a refusal that writes anything (digest differs) = **Blocker, class**; a plant that leaks state into other rows, or a row order dependence = **Major, class** (a leak seen only when a row fails midway = **Minor**); the builder's claim your run contradicts = **Major** if it hides a defect, **Minor** if only a number.
- **G-4 the answer (C5).** A first-half answer that differs between main's tree and the head's, or a second-half `detail` not byte-equal to `setPolicyTarget`'s, = **Major, class**; any product byte = **Blocker**. B724's CLOSED cells carried by blob equality are stated, not re-graded.
- **G-5 stability, CI, CodeQL (C6, C7).** A whole-suite red you reproduce twice = **Major**; the new file other than 17 of 17, or the groups other than 81/1509 (head tree) and main + 1 file + 17 tests (merge-equal), without a reason = a finding at the severity of its cause; names lost or added other than 0 / 8 = **Major**; lint/format/typecheck non-zero on the head and zero on main = **Major**; a load-only red = artefact (record both runs); a check-run `failure` whose annotation is the billing "job was not started" sentence = `CI pending: not scanned (job not started)`, a **condition**, never a finding on the code; a check-run failure with any other annotation or a started analysis with a finding = **Major** (an open alert on the head or merge ref = **Blocker** and a STOP); a textual conflict = **Major**; a path shared with #94, #91, #86, #85 or another live lane = **Major**; a merge ref still on other parents after 10 minutes of polling = a Note (recompute in your clone). **Always Note:** the author field, dependabot's vulnerabilities line, the squash artefact (the PR title becomes the squash subject), the contract notes not mentioning the refusal and the set-up card's pre-filled key (decisions N2 and N3 carried from B724, not graded here), D1 typecheck of the API test files (carried).
- **G-6 the verdict follows the table, and the cap.** Any Blocker, or any Major of the class = `NO GO round 2 of 2`: **this is the cap, no round 3**; FOR TUESDAY carries the CLOSED list (cells), the RESIDUE as ticket text with the tester's cells attached, and "a card to the product owner for a third round or a split landing". Notes and Minors only = `GO` or `GO WITH FOLLOW-UPS`; **because the hosted scan did not run, the best verdict is `GO WITH FOLLOW-UPS (conditional: CodeQL not scanned)`**; `CI pending` is always conditional. Add ` (conditional: <reason>)` for any required check not run.

## LOAD (binding; Composer docker route)
8 cores shared with other projects' seats (load1 read 8 to 17 at the draft; a Composer builder may start beside you). Heavy = `docker build`, any database-test container, the unit chain, any vitest over more than one file, the prober and dumper runs against postgres. **Start a heavy job only while `uptime` load1 is below 7 at two reads 4 s apart** (not independent reads: say so), recorded beside the result; at or over, poll every 20 s, log each wait, do light work meanwhile (C1, C2, the swap writer, the prober code, the clone, the C7 polls). **One heavy job of yours at a time**, behind `<project>/.tools/b743/lock` (copied `heavy.sh`; released by MOVE to `.tools/b743/quarantine/locks/`, never `rmdir`) and the cross-seat `ps` gate. A MOVING heartbeat (counter plus `date`) to `.tools/b743/logs/heartbeat.txt` every 30 s from every waiter and long job. A wait loop never uses `pgrep -f` on a pattern in its own command line (wait on a recorded PID, `wait $!`, or a done-marker file). Every command gets its input or none (`/dev/null`). NO artificial load. Build `pc-b743-node:head` once from the head's tree: `docker build --pull=false --progress=plain -f <tree>/docker/Dockerfile --target ci -t pc-b743-node:head <tree>` (an ABSOLUTE `-f`); record node, npm, vitest, tsc versions (RELAYED: v22.23.2, 10.9.8, vitest 5.0.0, tsc 5.9.3). One image serves main and the head only if the lockfile blobs are equal (no package byte moved; prove by `rev-parse` of both); build `pc-b743-node:main` only if `npm ci` of the second differs (say so). Plan the container starts (new file 3x, 17 rows alone, groups at head, main and the merge-equal tree, two unit runs, the prober at head and main, the swap table in 2-3 batches over 15 files, the old-file control batch) and write the budget at Step 0 (about 40). Remove ONLY your own `pc-b743-*` containers, networks and anonymous postgres volumes, by exact name.

## HOLDS
Datasec / Security Composer only; if any output shows another client's material, stop and disclose its shape. No deploy, `az`, Kudu, Entra, Graph, ssh. **No HTTP to any hosted or production host or the demo site** (the app under test runs in-process or in your own container with no published port). Never `docker exec`/`stop`/`rm`/`logs` against a container you did not create (the copied `dbtest.sh` execs into the database container it created itself). Network: your one in-clone `git fetch`, `gh api -X GET` under the project `GH_CONFIG_DIR`, nothing else; `gh run rerun`, `gh workflow run` and any POST/PUT/PATCH/DELETE are forbidden; never dismiss an alert. Git in the project repo `2_Project_Files`: READ verbs only (`--no-optional-locks`: ls-remote, log, show, diff, cat-file, ls-tree, rev-parse, rev-list, merge-base, grep, config --get); clone, fetch, worktree add, merge-tree only inside `.tools/b743/repo` and `.tools/wt-b743-*`. **HP-NDA hold:** never open `HP Reporting and Docs/`, any SOW, `1_Project_Definition/Source_Documents/` contents or `inbound/` folders. **The unit step's Essential Eight SOW text input is passed ONLY as a read-only bind mount into a `--network none` container, at the path the copied `unit.sh` already names (`PC_E8_SOW_TEXT`); stat it with `[ -f ]`; never open, print, grep, hash or quote it.** The Stamp slot "Stamped by" records Tuesday's `Q-2` answer; no answer reads NO, the bind mount is not made, and the unit rows that need the SOW text are NOT TESTED (the other unit steps still run). No decision-queue tool, scoreboard, Artifact, Docs, mail, chat or publish tool. Secrets only as environment; never open `4_Credentials/.env` except the NAME test, never `3_Access_Keys/`. **Never delete** (`rm`, `branch -D`, `reset`, `clean`, `stash`, `prune`, `rm -f` of any kind, `/dev/null` included): quarantine to `.tools/b743/quarantine/`. **Never `cd`**; absolute single-quoted paths (they hold a space and `!`); write `${VAR}:path`; no unquoted word starting with `=`; no unquoted `$VAR` holding a command with spaces; multi-step chains under `bash -c` or a quoted-heredoc script; `/usr/bin/grep -i` with a positive control for every count; `python3 -I` for anything reading a file you did not write; read your scripts back and scan for non-ASCII. Scratch changes (planted rows, swaps, the order-reversed copy) live ONLY in `wt-b743-mut`, `wt-b743-probe`, `.tools/b743/scratch/` and the throwaway test database; never in a committed file, never against a database that is not the throwaway container's. No person's name in any id, file or STATUS (say "the product owner"; do not quote git author fields), no card slug, clock from `date`. Nothing to any human. **STANDING LINES:** PRIOR-WORK CHECK (your STATUS carries a PRIOR WORK section naming what you read of the builder lanes (B712, B737) and the earlier gate (B724) and what you reuse; a READY-class verdict without one is returned); no message to any human; Jira writes none; never delete (quarantine). **RESUME at about 80% of context or at the hard stop:** write `PROGRESS` and `RESUME` sections (each check done/partial/not started with evidence paths; next commands; every scratch tree with its restore proof; lock released), stop your processes and containers, end `STOPPED: NEEDS TUESDAY` with the one question "continue in a fresh seat from RESUME?". **Usage pause:** if your session ends at the account's weekly limit, that is the platform, not a STOP; on resume re-read your own STATUS last line, re-pin main, the head and the checks, release or reclaim any lock you held by your own rule, and carry on against the hard stop Tuesday names in an addendum.

